{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08UQ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:18f01fb35501626b9f7ec868e304885b885cefe321e66fba75ef124c26555c48", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe fundamental triangle for the cotangent complex of sheaves of rings\nis an easy consequence of the result for homomorphisms of rings.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b4598e6f16e574e345dae8707848596f602c9677eb49f330eee56c2a57a3b588", "unit_id": "tag:08UQ:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08UQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nL_{\\mathcal{B}/\\mathcal{A}} \\otimes_\\mathcal{B}^\\mathbf{L} \\mathcal{C}\n\\to L_{\\mathcal{C}/\\mathcal{A}} \\to L_{\\mathcal{C}/\\mathcal{B}} \\to\nL_{\\mathcal{B}/\\mathcal{A}} \\otimes_\\mathcal{B}^\\mathbf{L} \\mathcal{C}[1]\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$D(\\mathcal{C})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-triangle-sheaves-rings}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8dea109f5e0ff6bb05754b261588130084ad64c3afef536532aa0b0df6ae5ca8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:832ebf0a054236c3668f33ad168891ab20ec56ab0f878c200c3ba222da5c7ff5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe homomorphisms of sheaves of rings on <MATH_0003>.\nThere is a canonical distinguished triangle\n<MATH_0004>\nin <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e3868410374a39a4aaa18ad36e628421d0943b8a8894f08ca4b51fbb05a0c3e6", "unit_id": "tag:08SZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08UQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Q}_\\bullet$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{R}_\\bullet$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{S}_\\bullet$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{Q}}_\\bullet =\n\\mathcal{Q}_\\bullet \\otimes_{\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet} \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{R}}_\\bullet =\n\\mathcal{R}_\\bullet \\otimes_{\\mathcal{S}_\\bullet} \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0017": "$$\n0 \\to\n\\Omega_{\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet/\\mathcal{A}}\n\\otimes_{\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet} \\mathcal{C} \\to\n\\Omega_{\\mathcal{Q}_\\bullet/\\mathcal{A}}\n\\otimes_{\\mathcal{Q}_\\bullet} \\mathcal{C} \\to\n\\Omega_{\\overline{\\mathcal{Q}}_\\bullet/\\mathcal{B}}\n\\otimes_{\\overline{\\mathcal{Q}}_\\bullet} \\mathcal{C} \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0018": "$L_{\\mathcal{C}/\\mathcal{B}}$", "MATH_0019": "$$\nL_{\\mathcal{C}/\\mathcal{B}} =\n\\Omega_{\\mathcal{R}_\\bullet/\\mathcal{B}}\n\\otimes_{\\mathcal{R}_\\bullet} \\mathcal{C}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Omega_{\\overline{\\mathcal{R}}_\\bullet/\\mathcal{B}}\n\\otimes_{\\overline{\\mathcal{R}}_\\bullet} \\mathcal{C}\n\\longleftarrow\n\\Omega_{\\overline{\\mathcal{Q}}_\\bullet/\\mathcal{B}}\n\\otimes_{\\overline{\\mathcal{Q}}_\\bullet} \\mathcal{C}\n$$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{A}(U) \\to \\mathcal{B}(U) \\to \\mathcal{C}(U)$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0023": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0024": "$\\mathcal{B} \\times \\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-triangle}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-explicit-map}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{remark-triangle}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-compute-L-product-sheaves-rings}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0009": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0010": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e71534e206d5f47b99278b1cb359c1ae370f061ee2853560ab3223c3b4a51e0c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e758c14acc4766e0d4b604f28d9e82763495d6913bdf1516af2ef0f37bd9ce13", "source_text": "We will use the method described in\nRemarks <REF_0001> and <REF_0002>\nto construct the triangle; we will freely use the results mentioned there.\nAs in those remarks we first construct the triangle in case\n<MATH_0001> is an injective map of sheaves of rings.\nIn this case we set\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is the standard resolution of <MATH_0003>\nover <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is the standard resolution of <MATH_0006>\nover <MATH_0007>,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0008> is the standard resolution of <MATH_0009>\nover <MATH_0010>,\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0011> is the standard resolution of <MATH_0012>\nover <MATH_0013>,\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0014>, and\n<STRUCT_0007> <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0008>\nThe distinguished triangle is the distinguished triangle associated\nto the short exact sequence\nof simplicial <MATH_0016>-modules\n<MATH_0017>\nThe first two terms are equal to the first two terms of the triangle\nof the statement of the lemma. The identification of the last term with\n<MATH_0018> uses the quasi-isomorphisms of complexes\n<MATH_0019>\nAll the constructions used above can first be done on the level\nof presheaves and then sheafified. Hence to prove sequences are exact,\nor that map are quasi-isomorphisms it suffices to prove the corresponding\nstatement for the ring maps\n<MATH_0020>\nwhich are known. This finishes the proof in the case that\n<MATH_0021> is injective.\n\n<STRUCT_0009><STRUCT_0010>\nIn general, we reduce to the case where <MATH_0022> is\ninjective by replacing <MATH_0023> by <MATH_0024> if\nnecessary. This is possible by the argument given in\nRemark <REF_0003> by\nLemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f1bc60fd4a11b9de1c1e63709e10dd0b7309d41c1acf0acb3c1c8f72d0c7240e", "unit_id": "tag:08SZ:proof"}
